<!--
  Material Symbols "add a photo", outlined — DESIGN.md §9, added by P2-17.

  Composed from the two glyphs this app already ships — the camera body of
  ic_photo_camera.xml and the plus of ic_add.xml — rather than a fourth party's
  path data, so the stroke weight and the corner radii match the other
  twenty-four exactly. A vector drawable rather than material-icons-core, which
  is not on the Compose classpath and would be a new dependency plus an I1
  clearance for a handful of glyphs. See ic_play_circle.xml, the first of these.

  Not ic_photo_camera itself: that glyph is already the drawer's "Intruder
  capture" row, three sections down the same sheet, and two rows in one drawer
  carrying one mark is the ambiguity §6.4 exists to prevent.
-->
